          "canonical_hash": "sha256:1e5cdbb15071eec5faf414c6ac5ad2b5aa0ed6feda026fe7e19000047145320b",
          "description": "PURPOSE: Step emulation by exactly N frames (default 1) and return the new framecount. USAGE: Use for frame-precise input automation (combine with bizhawk_press_buttons), animation inspection, or letting the system initialize after a hard reset (RAM is mostly zero in the first ~30 frames after bizhawk_reset). For long jumps (thousands of frames) prefer bizhawk_save_state / bizhawk_load_state of a pre-prepared state — frame_advance scales linearly. Works whether emulation is currently paused or running and does NOT change the pause state. BEHAVIOR: Advances the game-logic clock by N frames. Each step costs roughly one real frame (~16ms at 60Hz) plus one bridge round-trip — so advancing 600 frames takes ~10 seconds wall-clock. Returns an error if the loaded core doesn",
