          "canonical_hash": "sha256:a52aef6b08de03adfdcd8886e3bd1f27b7cf9915b90639ff7d8756d01eb6ad85",
          "description": "PURPOSE: Play a pre-built sequence of per-frame joypad inputs back-to-back, advancing one frame per element, ENTIRELY SERVER-SIDE in a single bridge round-trip. Optionally captures screenshots AND labeled memory reads at fixed frame intervals during the play, and optionally aborts play early when a specified memory address changes. All observations come back inline so the agent sees the full trajectory + game state in one tool response. USAGE: Use whenever you have ≥10 frames of inputs to play in order — TAS movie playback, scripted multi-frame sequences, AI-search of input patterns, agent-driven gameplay. ONE bridge round-trip ships N frames instead of the 2N round-trips you",
